In Castle of the Winds (my first Roguelike that I've ever played.
Before I knew what the term Roguelike actually meant :-p) there
is a nice gameplay feature that is currently missing from Nethack.
Mind you, I don't exactly remember how it works... but this is a
YANI anyway. I'll make it up the details as I forget them :-p

To be able to use a Wand, potion, scroll, and so forth, you
must spend 1 turn to take it out of your bag, and then 1 turn to
actually use it.

However; if the Wand, potion, etc. etc. was in your "free hand", or in
your utility belt, you could use it immediately. Of course, if you
wear a shield or use a 2x handed weapon, you don't have a free hand.

Utility belts can hold between 2 to 5 items, depending on what kind of
belt it is. Going by "Nethack physics", I'd say that they should hold
2 to 5 slots of stacked items. To make things more difficult, I'd
recommend to require daggers, darts, and so forth to also be
"readied" before they can be thrown.

So anyway, the new items would be 2-slot belts, 3 slot belts, and 5
slot utility belts. Without a belt, you could only [Q]uiver one
weapon/wand/scroll at a time. Belts seem to fit under "tools" catagory
pretty well (with BoH and sacks right there)

I don't intend for this to be a "realistic" YANI (no need to spend 5
turns searching for items) but it should add more strategy into the
game. With only a maximum of 6 items (5slot belt + shieldless hand)
that can be used in 1 turn (and less before midgame), you will have
to spend some time thinking over ready strategy.

Do you want your 50 poisoned arrows, /oTeleport, /oFire, /oDig, and
!oFullHealings, or should you swap out the arrows for daggers?
Darts? /oCancelation? Maybe you should take off that shield and
get that 6th slot open. Maybe as a Rogue, you'd prefer a mirror
at the ready to scare your enemies. Or the Bugle before entering
the Castle? When is it prime time to ready the /oDeath?

Maybe you should ready the lamp to conserve oil. (turn it off
in bright rooms).

I feel like such an addition would add not only to Nethack, but
to Slash'Em as well. But in Slash'Em, I suggest the Cloak
"TrenchCoat" with adds another 5 slots ontop of the belt. Or
maybe the ex/intrinsic "all ready" (gained by lvl 10 Rogues)
which means all items are always ready, and items inside a
belt take 1/2 time to use.

